Leave questions and messages for me here. Put new messages at the top; makes 'em easier to find.

----

LowPriorityStuff (an answer or decision next year is soon enough)

041117, BillStClair: Guess I missed a few. Thanks for fixing them. Nothing to worry about unless we find spam changes dated 11/17/2004 or later.

041117, JunkerIn: Ok. Hope it kills the spam. But note, so far Gulching, Utilitarianism And AnCap, & Low Priority Stuff found to be still spammed.

040905, MattisManzel: Hi Bill, sounds good. 

040522, JunkerIn: Sorry on the un-IDed change. I thought it had me logged in.

040122, JunkerIn, Suggestion: add automated outline page with links at page top with "AnCapWiki | RecentChanges | Preferences | Upload". outline would just be the linked titles of each page with single- or double-space indents for each level. a quick & easy recursion should do it. Oh, recurses! Foiled again!

:040121, BillStClair (yes, I can answer JunkerIn on the day before he posted, because he lives seven hours ahead of me, hehe): I like the idea of an outline page, and I think I can put it in the header and footer, but I don't know how to automate it short of writing lots of Perl code, which I'm not inclined to do. That leaves it as a task for a person, likely me, since I'm better at these kind of mindless tasks right now than at the actual writing, and I love how you're doing that and don't want to distract you with administrivia.

::still 040122, JunkerIn: 1) We *expect* more from the administrator. <g> 2. While it is not greatly important, I can convert to Central American Time. I used to report in Zulu time, i.e., GMT. 

::040122, BillStClair: 1) Gulp. 2) Heavens to Betsies. Don't worry about it...

040120, JunkerIn, re:  UseModSetup. saw it, thought it related to my ealier request since erased by me, in any case, it helps, thank you.

:040121, BillStClair: glad to hear it.

re: Ama-Gi & Stylesheet Project. to not be impolite, i'm not ignoring, i like both ama-gi's, but generally graphics & Stylesheet fancy I deem as ... unimportant? etc., etc. long diatribe on glitz ... so i'll generally abstain. And of course, your site, your call. i'm glad i can just be of some help.

:040121, BillStClair: understood. I'm lousy at creating graphics and style sheets, but I appreciate them when they're done well. Hence the projects, hoping that someone competent will step up. I don't want glitz either, but good design actually makes a site easier to read.

